-	 * We want to oversample enough to be sure that we will
-	 * have enough values with probability at least 1 - 2^(-256).
-	 * Depending on degree N, this leads to the following
-	 * required oversampling:
-	 *
-	 *   logn     n  oversampling
-	 *     1      2     65
-	 *     2      4     67
-	 *     3      8     71
-	 *     4     16     77
-	 *     5     32     86
-	 *     6     64    100
